<title>USA: Glickman - Russia interested in more US farm goods.</title>
<headline>Glickman - Russia interested in more US farm goods.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia, which had a poor grain harvest, is interested in making additional purchases of U.S. farm exports, U.S. Agriculture Secretary Dan Glickman said after meeting Thursday Deputy Prime Minister Alexander Zaveryukha.</p>
<p>&quot;While I can't comment specifically yet, I think there is some interest on their part to purchase additional American commodities,&quot; Glickman told reporters. &quot;Grains were mentioned, he said, but cautioned it all was &quot;generically mentioned so we didn't go into any kind of arrangements. Nothing imminent. Nothing to announce.&quot;  </p>
<p>Russia is the No. 1 market for U.S. poultry exports.</p>
<p>Glickman and Zaveruykha met as part of the semiannual Gore-Chernomyrdin commission meetings of top officials from both nations.</p>
<p>Glickman said he and Zaveryukha discussed the poultry trade as part of their discussions and also touched on possible joint ventures.</p>
</text>
